IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-mischief.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part XI (Wilful and Forbidden Acts in Respect of Certain Property): sections 428 to 432.
-- "property" in this Part is section 428's ("means real or personal corporeal property"), not section 2's. Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4.
-- Seams taken as inputs, named for the section that answers them: `s 342.1(2) computer data` (section 430(8)) and `s 318(4) identifiable group`.

§ `Part XI -- sections 428 to 432`

§§ `Interpretation and general provisions -- sections 428 and 429`

-- src:7618 | Interpretation
-- src:7619 | Definition of property
-- src:7620 | 428 In this Part, property means real or personal corporeal property.
@ref s 428 (src:7618-7620)
GIVEN `the thing is real or personal corporeal property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 428 property` MEANS
    IF `the thing is real or personal corporeal property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "property means real or personal corporeal property"

-- 429 (1) Every one who causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is his duty to do, knowing that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event and being reckless whether the event occurs or not, shall be deemed, for the purposes of this Part, wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event.
-- A deeming rule adds a case; it does not say that every other person is not wilful: NOTHING when its elements are unmet.
-- src:7621 | Wilfully causing event to occur
-- src:7622 | 429 (1) Every one who causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is his duty to do, knowing that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event and being reckless whether the event occurs or not, shall be deemed, for the purposes of this Part, wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event.
@ref s 429(1) (src:7621-7622)
GIVEN `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` MEANS
    IF `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` AND `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` AND `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection deems a case wilful and says nothing of a person who falls outside it

-- (2) A person shall not be convicted of an offence under sections 430 to 446 if they act with legal justification or excuse or colour of right.
-- src:7623 | Colour of right
-- src:7624 | (2) A person shall not be convicted of an offence under sections 430 to 446 if they act with legal justification or excuse or colour of right.
@ref s 429(2) (src:7623-7624)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person acts with legal justification or excuse or colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 429(2) the person shall not be convicted of the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence`'s section AT LEAST 430 AND `the offence`'s section AT MOST 446)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under sections 430 to 446"
    ELSE IF `the person acts with legal justification or excuse or colour of right`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if they act with legal justification or excuse or colour of right"

-- (3) Where it is an offence to destroy or to damage anything, (a) the fact that a person has a partial interest in what is destroyed or damaged does not prevent him from being guilty of the offence if he caused the destruction or damage; and
-- (b) the fact that a person has a total interest in what is destroyed or damaged does not prevent him from being guilty of the offence if he caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud.
-- src:7625 | Interest
-- src:7626 | (3) Where it is an offence to destroy or to damage anything,
-- src:7627 | (a) the fact that a person has a partial interest in what is destroyed or damaged does not prevent him from being guilty of the offence if he caused the destruction or damage; and
-- src:7628 | (b) the fact that a person has a total interest in what is destroyed or damaged does not prevent him from being guilty of the offence if he caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud.
@ref s 429(3) (src:7625-7628)
GIVEN `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a partial interest in what is destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person caused the destruction or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 429(3)(a) the person’s partial interest does not prevent guilt of the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is an offence to destroy or to damage anything"
    ELSE IF NOT `the person has a partial interest in what is destroyed or damaged`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of a partial interest
         ELSE IF `the person caused the destruction or damage`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he caused the destruction or damage"

@ref s 429(3)(b) (src:7627-7628)
GIVEN `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a total interest in what is destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 429(3)(b) the person’s total interest does not prevent guilt of the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is an offence to destroy or to damage anything"
    ELSE IF NOT `the person has a total interest in what is destroyed or damaged`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of a total interest
         ELSE IF `the person caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud"

§§ `Mischief -- section 430`

-- (8) In this section, computer data has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2). The text of subsection 342.1(2) is another part's (seam [T] of PLAN.md): its answer is an input.
-- src:7690 | Definition of computer data
-- src:7691 | (8) In this section, computer data has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2).
@ref s 430(8) (src:7690-7691)
GIVEN `s 342.1(2) computer data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(8) the thing is computer data` MEANS
    `s 342.1(2) computer data`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "computer data has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2)"; the answer is subsection 342.1(2)'s

-- (6) No person commits mischief within the meaning of this section by reason only that (a) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree on any matter relating to his employment;
-- (b) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and a bargaining agent acting on his behalf to agree on any matter relating to his employment; or (c) he stops work as a result of his taking part in a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection as workmen or employees.
-- src:7683 | Saving
-- src:7684 | (6) No person commits mischief within the meaning of this section by reason only that
-- src:7685 | (a) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree on any matter relating to his employment;
-- src:7686 | (b) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and a bargaining agent acting on his behalf to agree on any matter relating to his employment; or
-- src:7687 | (c) he stops work as a result of his taking part in a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection as workmen or employees.
@ref s 430(6) (src:7683-7687)
DECLARE `s 430(6) reason for stopping work` IS ONE OF
    `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment`   -- (a)
    `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and a bargaining agent acting on their behalf to agree on any matter relating to their employment`   -- (b)
    `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of their taking part in a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection as workmen or employees`   -- (c)
    `s 430(6) a stoppage of work for a reason that is none of those`

@ref s 430(6) (src:7683-7687)
GIVEN reason IS A `s 430(6) reason for stopping work`
      `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(6) the person is saved from committing mischief` MEANS
    IF reason EQUALS `s 430(6) a stoppage of work for a reason that is none of those`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving names paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)
    ELSE IF `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by reason only that"; this subsection gives no saving on these facts

-- (7) No person commits mischief within the meaning of this section by reason only that he attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information.
-- src:7688 | Idem
-- src:7689 | (7) No person commits mischief within the meaning of this section by reason only that he attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information.
@ref s 430(7) (src:7688-7689)
GIVEN `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(7) the person is saved from committing mischief` MEANS
    IF `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` AND `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information"; this subsection gives no saving on these facts

DECLARE `s 430(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 430(1) destroys or damages property`   -- (a)
    `s 430(1) renders property dangerous, useless, inoperative or ineffective`   -- (b)
    `s 430(1) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with the lawful use, enjoyment or operation of property`   -- (c)
    `s 430(1) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with any person in the lawful use, enjoyment or operation of property`   -- (d)
    `s 430(1) an act that is none of those, in relation to property`

-- 430 (1) Every one commits mischief who wilfully (a) destroys or damages property; (b) renders property dangerous, useless, inoperative or ineffective; (c) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with the lawful use, enjoyment or operation of property; or (d) obstructs ... any person in the lawful use ... of property.
-- src:7630 | Mischief
-- src:7631 | Mischief
-- src:7632 | 430 (1) Every one commits mischief who wilfully
-- src:7633 | (a) destroys or damages property;
-- src:7634 | (b) renders property dangerous, useless, inoperative or ineffective;
-- src:7635 | (c) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with the lawful use, enjoyment or operation of property; or
-- src:7636 | (d) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with any person in the lawful use, enjoyment or operation of property.
@ref s 430(1) (src:7630-7636)
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is wilful because it is deemed so, by s 429(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 430(1) act`
      `the thing is property, by s 428` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the saving applies, by s 430(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the saving applies, by s 430(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(1) the conduct is mischief in relation to property` MEANS
    IF NOT (act EQUALS `s 430(1) an act that is none of those, in relation to property`)
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `ccc13 any of` (LIST JUST `the person acts wilfully`, `the act is wilful because it is deemed so, by s 429(1)`)
                            , `the thing is property, by s 428`
                            , `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 430(6)`
                            , `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 430(7)`)
         -- NOTHING for "wilfully" when it is neither shown nor deemed, as s 429(1) answers NOTHING outside its case; JUST FALSE when the thing is not property (the "means" of section 428) or a saving applies
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits mischief who wilfully"

DECLARE `s 430(1.1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data`   -- (a)
    `s 430(1.1) renders computer data meaningless, useless or ineffective`   -- (b)
    `s 430(1.1) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with the lawful use of computer data`   -- (c)
    `s 430(1.1) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with a person in the lawful use of computer data or denies access to computer data to a person who is entitled to access to it`   -- (d)
    `s 430(1.1) an act that is none of those, in relation to computer data`

-- src:7637 | Mischief in relation to computer data
-- src:7638 | (1.1) Everyone commits mischief who wilfully
-- src:7639 | (a) destroys or alters computer data;
-- src:7640 | (b) renders computer data meaningless, useless or ineffective;
-- src:7641 | (c) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with the lawful use of computer data; or
-- src:7642 | (d) obstructs, interrupts or interferes with a person in the lawful use of computer data or denies access to computer data to a person who is entitled to access to it.
@ref s 430(1.1) (src:7637-7642)
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is wilful because it is deemed so, by s 429(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 430(1.1) act`
      `the thing is computer data, by s 430(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the saving applies, by s 430(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the saving applies, by s 430(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(1.1) the conduct is mischief in relation to computer data` MEANS
    IF NOT (act EQUALS `s 430(1.1) an act that is none of those, in relation to computer data`)
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `ccc13 any of` (LIST JUST `the person acts wilfully`, `the act is wilful because it is deemed so, by s 429(1)`)
                            , `the thing is computer data, by s 430(8)`
                            , `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 430(6)`
                            , `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 430(7)`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits mischief who wilfully"

-- (2) Every one who commits mischief that causes actual danger to life is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
-- src:7643 | Punishment
-- src:7644 | (2) Every one who commits mischief that causes actual danger to life is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 430(2) (src:7643-7644)
GIVEN `the person commits mischief, by s 430(1) or (1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the mischief causes actual danger to life` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(2) the conduct is the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life` MEANS
    IF `the mischief causes actual danger to life`
    THEN `the person commits mischief, by s 430(1) or (1.1)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who commits mischief that causes actual danger to life"

@ref s 430(2) (the punishments) (src:7643-7644)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 430(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 430(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7643-7644)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 430(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- (3) Every one who commits mischief in relation to property that is a testamentary instrument or the value of which exceeds five thousand dollars; (4) ... in relation to property, other than property described in subsection (3).
-- src:7645 | Punishment
-- src:7646 | (3) Every one who commits mischief in relation to property that is a testamentary instrument or the value of which exceeds five thousand dollars
-- src:7647 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:7648 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 430(3) (src:7645-7648)
GIVEN `the property is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the value of the property, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(3) the property is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars` MEANS
    `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the property is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument`, JUST (`the value of the property, in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000))
    -- JUST FALSE when neither: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "property that is a testamentary instrument or the value of which exceeds five thousand dollars"

@ref s 430(3) (the offence) (src:7645-7648)
GIVEN `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is described in subsection (3), by s 430(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(3) the conduct is the offence of mischief in relation to property of great value` MEANS
    `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)`, `the property is described in subsection (3), by s 430(3)`)

@ref s 430(3) (the punishments) (src:7645-7648)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 430(3) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 430(3) (the class of the offence) (src:7645-7648)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 430(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7649 | Idem
-- src:7650 | (4) Every one who commits mischief in relation to property, other than property described in subsection (3),
-- src:7651 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:7652 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 430(4) (src:7649-7652)
GIVEN `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is described in subsection (3), by s 430(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(4) the conduct is the offence of mischief in relation to other property` MEANS
    `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)`, `ccc13 not` `the property is described in subsection (3), by s 430(3)`)

@ref s 430(4) (the punishments) (src:7649-7652)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 430(4) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 430(4) (the class of the offence) (src:7649-7652)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 430(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4.101) For the purposes of subsection (4.1), property means (a) a building or structure ... primarily used for religious worship ... or a cemetery; (b) ... primarily used by an identifiable group as defined in subsection 318(4) as an educational institution ...;
-- (c) ... for administrative, social, cultural or sports activities or events ...; or (d) ... as a residence for seniors or an object associated with that residence ...
-- src:7657 | Definition of property
-- src:7658 | (4.101) For the purposes of subsection (4.1), property means
-- src:7659 | (a) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used for religious worship — including a church, mosque, synagogue or temple —, an object associated with religious worship located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure, or a cemetery;
-- src:7660 | (b) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as defined in subsection 318(4) as an educational institution — including a school, daycare centre, college or university —, or an object associated with that institution located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure;
-- src:7661 | (c) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as defined in subsection 318(4) for administrative, social, cultural or sports activities or events — including a town hall, community centre, playground or arena —, or an object associated with such an activity or event located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure; or
-- src:7662 | (d) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as defined in subsection 318(4) as a residence for seniors or an object associated with that residence located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure.
@ref s 430(4.101) (src:7657-7662)
DECLARE `s 430(4.101) kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `s 430(4.101) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used for religious worship, an object associated with religious worship located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure, or a cemetery`   -- (a)
    `s 430(4.101) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as an educational institution, or an object associated with that institution located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure`   -- (b)
    `s 430(4.101) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group for administrative, social, cultural or sports activities or events, or an object associated with such an activity or event located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure`   -- (c)
    `s 430(4.101) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as a residence for seniors or an object associated with that residence located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure`   -- (d)
    `s 430(4.101) property that is none of those`

@ref s 430(4.101) (src:7657-7662)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 430(4.101) kind of property`
      `the group is an identifiable group, as defined in subsection 318(4), by s 318(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(4.101) the property is property for the purposes of subsection (4.1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 430(4.101) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used for religious worship, an object associated with religious worship located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure, or a cemetery` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 430(4.101) property that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of subsection (4.1), property means"
    OTHERWISE `the group is an identifiable group, as defined in subsection 318(4), by s 318(4)`   -- (b), (c), (d): JUST TRUE for an identifiable group; the answer of s 318(4) otherwise

-- (4.1) Everyone who commits mischief in relation to property described in any of paragraphs (4.101)(a) to (d), if the commission of the mischief is motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression or mental or physical disability.
-- src:7653 | Mischief relating to religious property, educational institutions, etc.
-- src:7654 | (4.1) Everyone who commits mischief in relation to property described in any of paragraphs (4.101)(a) to (d), if the commission of the mischief is motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression or mental or physical disability,
-- src:7655 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:7656 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 430(4.1) (src:7653-7656)
GIVEN `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is property for the purposes of subsection (4.1), by s 430(4.101)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the commission of the mischief is motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression or mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(4.1) the conduct is the offence of mischief motivated by bias in relation to religious property, educational institutions, etc.` MEANS
    IF `the commission of the mischief is motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression or mental or physical disability`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)`, `the property is property for the purposes of subsection (4.1), by s 430(4.101)`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the commission of the mischief is motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression or mental or physical disability"

@ref s 430(4.1) (the punishments) (src:7653-7656)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 430(4.1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 430(4.1) (the class of the offence) (src:7653-7656)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 430(4.1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4.11) ... guilty of an indictable offence or an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable, (a) whether prosecuted by indictment or punishable on summary conviction, to the following minimum punishment, namely, (i) for a first offence, to a fine of not less than $1,000,
-- (ii) for a second offence, to imprisonment for not less than 14 days, and (iii) for each subsequent offence, to imprisonment for not less than 30 days; (b) if prosecuted by indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years; and (c) if punishable on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day.
-- src:7663 | Mischief relating to war memorials
-- src:7664 | (4.11) Everyone who commits mischief in relation to property that is a building, structure or part thereof that primarily serves as a monument to honour persons who were killed or died as a consequence of a war, including a war memorial or cenotaph, or an object associated with honouring or remembering those persons that is located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure, or a cemetery is guilty of an indictable offence or an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable,
-- src:7665 | (a) whether the offence is prosecuted by indictment or punishable on summary conviction, to the following minimum punishment, namely,
-- src:7666 | (i) for a first offence, to a fine of not less than $1,000,
-- src:7667 | (ii) for a second offence, to imprisonment for not less than 14 days, and
-- src:7668 | (iii) for each subsequent offence, to imprisonment for not less than 30 days;
-- src:7669 | (b) if the offence is prosecuted by indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years; and
-- src:7670 | (c) if the offence is punishable on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day.
@ref s 430(4.11) (src:7663-7670)
GIVEN `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is a building, structure or part thereof that primarily serves as a monument to honour persons who were killed or died as a consequence of a war, including a war memorial or cenotaph, an object associated with honouring or remembering those persons located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure, or a cemetery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(4.11) the conduct is the offence of mischief in relation to war memorials` MEANS
    IF `the property is a building, structure or part thereof that primarily serves as a monument to honour persons who were killed or died as a consequence of a war, including a war memorial or cenotaph, an object associated with honouring or remembering those persons located in or on the grounds of such a building or structure, or a cemetery`
    THEN `the person commits mischief in relation to property, by s 430(1)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone who commits mischief in relation to property that is a building, structure or part thereof that primarily serves as a monument to honour persons who were killed or died as a consequence of a war"

-- The minimum depends on whether this is a first, a second or a later offence: the number is a fact the person states (1, 2, 3 or more).
@ref s 430(4.11) (the punishments) (src:7663-7670)
GIVEN `the number of the offence: 1 for a first offence, 2 for a second, 3 or more for each subsequent offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 430(4.11) the punishments` MEANS
    IF `the number of the offence: 1 for a first offence, 2 for a second, 3 or more for each subsequent offence` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text counts a first, a second and each subsequent offence; a number below one is none of them
    ELSE IF `the number of the offence: 1 for a first offence, 2 for a second, 3 or more for each subsequent offence` EQUALS 1
         THEN JUST (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `a fine of` 1000)   -- (a)(i), (b)
                       , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `a fine of` 1000))   -- (a)(i), (c)
         ELSE IF `the number of the offence: 1 for a first offence, 2 for a second, 3 or more for each subsequent offence` EQUALS 2
              THEN JUST (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (a)(ii), (b)
                            , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`))   -- (a)(ii), (c)
              ELSE JUST (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (a)(iii), (b)
                            , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`))   -- (a)(iii), (c)

@ref s 430(4.11) (the class of the offence) (src:7663-7670)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 430(4.11) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4.2) Every one who commits mischief in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention for the Protection of Cultural Property in the Event of Armed Conflict, done at The Hague on May 14, 1954, as set out in the schedule to the Cultural Property Export and Import Act.
