§§ `Attacks and devices -- sections 431 to 431.2`

-- src:7692 | Attack on premises, residence or transport of internationally protected person
-- src:7693 | 431 Every one who commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of an internationally protected person that is likely to endanger the life or liberty of such a person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than fourteen years.
@ref s 431 (src:7692-7693)
GIVEN `the person commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attack is likely to endanger the life or liberty of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attacked is an internationally protected person, by s 2 internationally protected person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431 the conduct is the offence of an attack on the premises, residence or transport of an internationally protected person` MEANS
    IF `the person commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of the person` AND `the attack is likely to endanger the life or liberty of such a person`
    THEN `the person attacked is an internationally protected person, by s 2 internationally protected person`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of an internationally protected person that is likely to endanger the life or liberty of such a person"

@ref s 431 (the punishments) (src:7692-7693)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 431 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 431 (the class of the offence) (src:7692-7693)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 431 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:7694 | Attack on premises, accommodation or transport of United Nations or associated personnel
-- src:7695 | 431.1 Every one who commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel that is likely to endanger the life or liberty of such a person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than fourteen years.
@ref s 431.1 (src:7694-7695)
GIVEN `the person commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attack is likely to endanger the life or liberty of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attacked is a member of United Nations personnel, by s 2 United Nations personnel` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person attacked is associated personnel, by s 2 associated personnel` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.1 the conduct is the offence of an attack on the premises, accommodation or transport of United Nations or associated personnel` MEANS
    IF `the person commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of the person` AND `the attack is likely to endanger the life or liberty of such a person`
    THEN `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the person attacked is a member of United Nations personnel, by s 2 United Nations personnel`, `the person attacked is associated personnel, by s 2 associated personnel`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who commits a violent attack on the official premises, private accommodation or means of transport of a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel"

@ref s 431.1 (the punishments) (src:7694-7695)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 431.1 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 431.1 (the class of the offence) (src:7694-7695)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 431.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- 431.2 (1) The following definitions apply in this section. Each term is a function; every one says "means", so the case outside it is JUST FALSE (the "means ... and includes" of "place of public use" is read as closed: fork F2 of the keel).
-- src:7696 | Definitions
-- src:7697 | 431.2 (1) The following definitions apply in this section.
-- src:7698 | explosive or other lethal device means
-- src:7699 | (a) an explosive or incendiary weapon or device that is designed to cause, or is capable of causing, death, serious bodily injury or substantial material damage; or
-- src:7700 | (b) a weapon or device that is designed to cause, or is capable of causing, death, serious bodily injury or substantial material damage through the release, dissemination or impact of toxic chemicals, biological agents or toxins or similar substances, or radiation or radioactive material. (engin explosif ou autre engin meurtrier)
@ref s 431.2(1) "explosive or other lethal device" (src:7696-7700)
DECLARE `s 431.2(1) kind of device` IS ONE OF
    `s 431.2(1) an explosive or incendiary weapon or device`   -- (a)
    `s 431.2(1) a weapon or device that causes harm through the release, dissemination or impact of toxic chemicals, biological agents or toxins or similar substances, or radiation or radioactive material`   -- (b)
    `s 431.2(1) a device that is neither`

@ref s 431.2(1) "explosive or other lethal device" (src:7698-7700)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 431.2(1) kind of device`
      `it is designed to cause, or is capable of causing, death, serious bodily injury or substantial material damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.2(1) the device is an explosive or other lethal device` MEANS
    IF (NOT (kind EQUALS `s 431.2(1) a device that is neither`)) AND `it is designed to cause, or is capable of causing, death, serious bodily injury or substantial material damage`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "explosive or other lethal device means"

-- src:7701 | infrastructure facility means a publicly or privately owned facility that provides or distributes services for the benefit of the public, including services relating to water, sewage, energy, fuel and communications. (infrastructure)
@ref s 431.2(1) "infrastructure facility" (src:7701-7701)
GIVEN `it is a publicly or privately owned facility that provides or distributes services for the benefit of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.2(1) the facility is an infrastructure facility` MEANS
    IF `it is a publicly or privately owned facility that provides or distributes services for the benefit of the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "infrastructure facility means a publicly or privately owned facility that provides or distributes services for the benefit of the public"

-- src:7702 | military forces of a state means the armed forces that a state organizes, trains and equips in accordance with the law of the state for the primary purpose of national defence or national security, and every person acting in support of those armed forces who is under their formal command, control and responsibility. (forces armées d’un État)
@ref s 431.2(1) "military forces of a state" (src:7702-7702)
GIVEN `they are the armed forces that a state organizes, trains and equips in accordance with the law of the state for the primary purpose of national defence or national security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are a person acting in support of those armed forces who is under their formal command, control and responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.2(1) the body or person is the military forces of a state` MEANS
    IF `they are the armed forces that a state organizes, trains and equips in accordance with the law of the state for the primary purpose of national defence or national security` OR `they are a person acting in support of those armed forces who is under their formal command, control and responsibility`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "military forces of a state means the armed forces that a state organizes, trains and equips in accordance with the law of the state"

-- src:7703 | place of public use means those parts of land, a building, street, waterway or other location that are accessible or open to members of the public, whether on a continuous, periodic or occasional basis, and includes any commercial, business, cultural, historical, educational, religious, governmental, entertainment, recreational or other place that is accessible or open to the public on such a basis. (lieu public)
@ref s 431.2(1) "place of public use" (src:7703-7703)
GIVEN `it is a part of land, a building, street, waterway or other location that is accessible or open to members of the public, whether on a continuous, periodic or occasional basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.2(1) the place is a place of public use` MEANS
    IF `it is a part of land, a building, street, waterway or other location that is accessible or open to members of the public, whether on a continuous, periodic or occasional basis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "place of public use means those parts of land, a building, street, waterway or other location that are accessible or open to members of the public"

-- src:7704 | public transportation system means a publicly or privately owned facility, conveyance or other thing that is used in connection with publicly available services for the transportation of persons or cargo. (système de transport public)
@ref s 431.2(1) "public transportation system" (src:7704-7704)
GIVEN `it is a publicly or privately owned facility, conveyance or other thing that is used in connection with publicly available services for the transportation of persons or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.2(1) the thing is a public transportation system` MEANS
    IF `it is a publicly or privately owned facility, conveyance or other thing that is used in connection with publicly available services for the transportation of persons or cargo`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "public transportation system means a publicly or privately owned facility, conveyance or other thing that is used in connection with publicly available services for the transportation of persons or cargo"

-- (3) For greater certainty, subsection (2) does not apply to an act or omission that is committed during an armed conflict and that, at the time and in the place of its commission, is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict,
-- or to activities undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law.
-- src:7707 | Armed forces
-- src:7708 | (3) For greater certainty, subsection (2) does not apply to an act or omission that is committed during an armed conflict and that, at the time and in the place of its commission, is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict, or to activities undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law.
@ref s 431.2(3) (src:7707-7708)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed during an armed conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time and in the place of its commission it is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is undertaken by military forces of a state, by s 431.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the activity is undertaken in the exercise of their official duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is governed by other rules of international law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.2(3) subsection (2) does not apply to the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission is committed during an armed conflict` AND `at the time and in the place of its commission it is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the activity is undertaken in the exercise of their official duties` AND `the activity is governed by other rules of international law`
         THEN `the activity is undertaken by military forces of a state, by s 431.2(1)`
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (2) does not apply to an act or omission that is committed during an armed conflict"; this subsection gives no saving on these facts

-- (2) Every one who delivers, places, discharges or detonates an explosive or other lethal device to, into, in or against a place of public use, a government or public facility, a public transportation system or an infrastructure facility,
-- either with intent to cause death or serious bodily injury or with intent to cause extensive destruction of such a place, system or facility that results in or is likely to result in major economic loss, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
-- src:7705 | Explosive or other lethal device
-- src:7706 | (2) Every one who delivers, places, discharges or detonates an explosive or other lethal device to, into, in or against a place of public use, a government or public facility, a public transportation system or an infrastructure facility, either with intent to cause death or serious bodily injury or with intent to cause extensive destruction of such a place, system or facility that results in or is likely to result in major economic loss, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 431.2(2) (src:7705-7706)
GIVEN `the person delivers, places, discharges or detonates the device to, into, in or against the place, facility or system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device is an explosive or other lethal device, by s 431.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the target is a place of public use, by s 431.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the target is a government or public facility, by s 2 government or public facility` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the target is a public transportation system, by s 431.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the target is an infrastructure facility, by s 431.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to cause death or serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to cause extensive destruction of such a place, system or facility that results in or is likely to result in major economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsection does not apply, by s 431.2(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 431.2(2) the conduct is the offence of delivering an explosive or other lethal device` MEANS
    IF `the person delivers, places, discharges or detonates the device to, into, in or against the place, facility or system` AND (`the person acts with intent to cause death or serious bodily injury` OR `the person acts with intent to cause extensive destruction of such a place, system or facility that results in or is likely to result in major economic loss`)
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the device is an explosive or other lethal device, by s 431.2(1)`
                            , `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the target is a place of public use, by s 431.2(1)`, `the target is a government or public facility, by s 2 government or public facility`, `the target is a public transportation system, by s 431.2(1)`, `the target is an infrastructure facility, by s 431.2(1)`)
                            , `ccc13 not` `the subsection does not apply, by s 431.2(3)`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who delivers, places, discharges or detonates an explosive or other lethal device to, into, in or against a place of public use"

@ref s 431.2(2) (the punishments) (src:7705-7706)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 431.2(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 431.2(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7705-7706)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 431.2(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

