-- (3) In addition to any punishment that is imposed on a person who is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may order that anything that is used in the commission of the offence be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings are taken.
-- src:7717 | Forfeiture
-- src:7718 | (3) In addition to any punishment that is imposed on a person who is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may order that anything that is used in the commission of the offence be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings are taken. Anything that is forfeited may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref s 432(3) (src:7717-7718)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no order may be made, by s 432(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 432(3) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province` MEANS
    IF `no order may be made, by s 432(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No order may be made under subsection (3) in respect of anything that is the property of a person who is not a party to the offence"
    ELSE IF `the person is convicted of an offence under this section` AND `the thing is used in the commission of the offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on a person who is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may order that anything that is used in the commission of the offence be forfeited"

DECLARE `s 432(3) act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 432(3) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province`

@ref s 432(3) (the power of the court) (src:7717-7718)
GIVEN `the court may order forfeiture, by s 432(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 432(3) act of the court`
`s 432(3) the power of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court may order forfeiture, by s 432(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 432(3) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 432 (1) A person who, without the consent of the theatre manager, records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work within the meaning of section 2 of the Copyright Act or its soundtrack (a) ... two years; or (b) summary conviction.
-- src:7709 | Unauthorized recording of a movie
-- src:7710 | 432 (1) A person who, without the consent of the theatre manager, records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work within the meaning of section 2 of the Copyright Act or its soundtrack
-- src:7711 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:7712 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 432(1) (src:7709-7712)
GIVEN `the person acts without the consent of the theatre manager` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work within the meaning of section 2 of the Copyright Act, or its soundtrack` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 432(1) the conduct is the offence of unauthorized recording of a movie` MEANS
    IF `the person acts without the consent of the theatre manager` AND `the person records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work within the meaning of section 2 of the Copyright Act, or its soundtrack`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who, without the consent of the theatre manager, records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work"

@ref s 432(1) (the punishments) (src:7709-7712)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 432(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 432(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7709-7712)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 432(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7713 | Unauthorized recording for purpose of sale, etc.
-- src:7714 | (2) A person who, without the consent of the theatre manager, records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work within the meaning of section 2 of the Copyright Act or its soundtrack for the purpose of the sale, rental or other commercial distribution of a copy of the cinematographic work
-- src:7715 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7716 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 432(2) (src:7713-7716)
GIVEN `the person acts without the consent of the theatre manager` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work within the meaning of section 2 of the Copyright Act, or its soundtrack` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the sale, rental or other commercial distribution of a copy of the cinematographic work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 432(2) the conduct is the offence of unauthorized recording of a movie for the purpose of sale` MEANS
    IF `the person acts without the consent of the theatre manager` AND `the person records in a movie theatre a performance of a cinematographic work within the meaning of section 2 of the Copyright Act, or its soundtrack` AND `the purpose is the sale, rental or other commercial distribution of a copy of the cinematographic work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purpose of the sale, rental or other commercial distribution of a copy of the cinematographic work"

@ref s 432(2) (the punishments) (src:7713-7716)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 432(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 432(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7713-7716)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 432(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
